1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,500
One plaza is a proof.

2
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:05,075
A city is the real question.

3
00:00:05,075 --> 00:00:12,900
So we hand CoolSpend a single instruction: spend a million euros, anywhere in Barcelona, where it relieves the most people.

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:26,987
It starts from the satellite map — ranks all four hundred ninety-four vulnerability cells, then drops a two-hundred by two-hundred metre sample over the highest-priority candidates and evaluates each one live, on real Infrared comfort fields.

5
00:00:26,987 --> 00:00:35,262
A hard rule keeps it honest: no single site may take more than a hundred and fifty thousand euros — so it can never saturate one plaza.

6
00:00:35,262 --> 00:00:41,375
It funds the best cost-per-square-metre first, spreads sites apart, and stops on its own.

7
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:59,600
The result: nine hundred thousand euros committed; ninety trees across six separated sites; a measured twenty thousand, six hundred and nine square metres cooled; about twenty-six thousand, seven hundred and forty-five residents reached inside a three-hundred-metre walk — counted once, not twice.

8
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:03,000
Forty-four euros per square metre cooled.

9
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:09,200
The mix is drawn entirely from the plantable palette: zero invasive, zero London plane.

10
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:13,350
The remaining hundred thousand stays uncommitted, by design.

11
00:01:13,350 --> 00:01:16,750
This is the answer a Chief Heat Officer can sign.

